    "created_at": "2026-07-04T12:01:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-04T12:01:23Z",
    "body": "I\u2019m not sure if I described this a bit clumsily above, but the issue is this: even though Beszel\u2019s graphs have been tweaked to fit smaller spaces, they still look extremely jagged to me.\n\n<img width=\"1008\" height=\"330\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f38bb75d-99b8-4baf-8fe0-63afd0b3be81\" />\n\nDashdot\u2019s graphs worked perfectly back in the day (see the images above), so I really have to wonder\u2014since graphs essentially just consist of x and y values, why new graphing systems have to be created instead of simply using the ones from Dashdot.\n\nFor me, this feature would be considered \"done\" if I could take the values \u200b\u200bfrom Beszel and plug them into, or view them within Dashdot\u2019s graphs.",
